      "writtenOn": "2025-10-01T11:51:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e It will be detected by kvm_set_cpuid(e2)-\u003ekvm_check_cpuid(e2), and returned before we set vcpu-\u003earch.cpuid_entries \u003d e2. So the pkvm hypervisor will not take the new vcpuid entries in this case\n\nAh, indeed. Seems all good then.\n\nJust one request: these details seem not quite obvious, so maybe let\u0027s add some comments to the code:\n1. Before the `percpu_fpstate` declaration, explain what you explained above, e.g.: \"percpu_fstate is used to reset the FPU hardware with the initial FPU state before switching from pVM to host, so that the host cannot get pVM\u0027s FPU contents\" + an explanation why it is guaranteed that the dynamic part of percpu_fpstate-\u003eregs will not be used so it\u0027s ok to allocate percpu_fpstate statically.\n2. When checking for \"size \u003c fpu_kernel_cfg.default_size + ...\" e.g. in donate_fpu(), explain that this is only the absolute required minimum, and we may actually require more (up to fpu_kernel_cfg.max_size + ...), which will be checked later by fpu_enable_guest_xfd_features() which will return -ENOMEM if needed?",
      "parentUuid": "644d0d3c_e9e694b8",
